{
  "id": "loser-effect",
  "term": "loser effect",
  "definition": "The loser effect is a self-reinforcing pattern in which an individual that loses a fight becomes more likely to lose again in later encounters. In studies of dominance hierarchies, this repeated effect can help produce stable, often linear rank orders within a group.",
